{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>You shall not take vengeance.</b> He said to him: Lend me your sickle. He said to him: No. The next day he said to him: Lend me your axe. He said to him: I am not lending to you, just as you did not lend to me — this is נְקִימָה. And which is נְטִירָה? He said to him: Lend me your axe. He said to him: No. The next day he said to him: Lend me your sickle. He said to him: Here, take it — I am not like you, who did not lend to me — this is נְטִירָה, that he harbors hatred in his heart even though he does not take vengeance (Sifra; Yoma 23)." "<b>And you shall love your fellow as yourself.</b> Rabbi Akiva said: This is a great principle in the Torah (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:09.058353833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}